This skill studies RMCProfile (https://rmcprofile.ornl.gov/), the Reverse
Monte Carlo program for total scattering developed at ORNL, ISIS, Oxford,
QMUL, NIST and Warsaw. It contains no code from that package: the file
formats are implemented from the published manual, the analysis routines
from the published method papers cited in references/method.md. The driver
in scripts/rmcprofile_tools.py runs a copy of RMCProfile that you download
and install yourself under its own terms
("AS IS and for non-profit making purposes", https://rmcprofile.ornl.gov/disclaimer/);
that copy and its tutorial files are never redistributed by this project.

